## S8 Post-checks

After the router returns, confirm that it has booted the approved IOS-XE image.
Repeat the interface and BGP checks recorded during S2 and compare the results with the pre-change baseline.
Confirm that expected interfaces are operational and expected BGP neighbours have returned to their previous healthy state.

Commands:
`show version`
`show ip interface brief`
`show ip bgp summary`

The upgrade is not considered successful until the post-check results are consistent with the approved pre-change baseline.

## S9 Rollback criteria

Start the backout process if the router fails to boot the approved image or if critical post-checks fail.
Rollback must also be considered when important interfaces do not recover, expected BGP neighbours remain unavailable, or the device shows repeated instability after the upgrade.

Do not improvise a recovery procedure.

Follow:
`RB-003: Rollback After Failed IOS-XE Upgrade`

The engineer responsible for the change must record the reason that rollback was triggered.

## S10 Closure and soak period

Record the final IOS-XE version and the outcome of all post-checks in the change record.
Record whether the upgrade completed successfully or required rollback.
Continue normal monitoring during a 14-day soak period for unexpected instability associated with the new software.

The change can be fully closed after the required evidence has been recorded and the applicable change-management process has been completed.